I tried to find something similar to this in the issue set but figured it was worth a new one:

This code triggers an odd `RuntimeWarning` at import time:

```python
from dataclasses import dataclass

from pydantic import BaseModel


@dataclass
class C:
    _private: str = 'yo'


class D(BaseModel):
    c: C = None
    
    class Config:
        arbitrary_types_allowed = True
        validate_all = False
        keep_untouched = (C,)
        underscore_attrs_are_private = False

```
running this code gives:
```
[nav] In [9]: run snippets/pydantic_warning.py
